            <ArticleTitle>Effect on lipoproteins of Trisequens, a combined hormone preparation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>279-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lipoprotein concentrations were measured in 31 post-menopausal women during 1 yr of treatment with Trisequens, a natural oestrogen-progestogen preparation. Serum triglyceride, high density lipoprotein and very low density lipoprotein cholesterol concentrations did not change significantly, but low density lipoprotein cholesterol concentrations fell over the first 6 mth. After 1 yr none of the lipoprotein fractions differed significantly in concentration from pre-treatment levels.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
